usage: with_argbind.py [-h] [--args.save ARGS.SAVE] [--args.load ARGS.LOAD]
                       [--args.debug ARGS.DEBUG]
                       [--configure.mode {train,val,test}]
                       [--configure.level {1,2,3}]
                       [--configure.backend {cpu,gpu}]

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --args.save ARGS.SAVE
                        Path to save all arguments used to run script to.
  --args.load ARGS.LOAD
                        Path to load arguments from, stored as a .yml file.
  --args.debug ARGS.DEBUG
                        Print arguments as they are passed to each function.

Generated arguments for function configure:
  Configure a run using Literal-restricted arguments.

  --configure.mode {train,val,test}
                        Which split to run, by default 'train'.
  --configure.level {1,2,3}
                        An integer level, by default 1.
  --configure.backend {cpu,gpu}
                        Optional compute backend; None lets the program decide, by
                        default None.
